  "detailed_description": "The scheme &amp;quot;Scheme to Provide Stipend to the Persons With Disabilities of the State for Poultry Training&amp;quot; by the Agriculture and Co-operation Department, Government of Gujarat, aims to provide financial assistance and capacity building to physically disabled individuals of the state by equipping them with poultry rearing skills. Under this scheme, eligible beneficiaries receive a stipend of ₹2,000/- for participating in a 7-day training session on poultry farming conducted by the Intensive Poultry Development Unit. The initiative is designed to enhance income opportunities and livelihood development for the physically disabled population across Gujarat.\n<br>\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n  - The applicant should be a resident of Gujarat.\n  - The applicant should be a person with physical disabilities, holding a valid PH Identity Card.\n  - The applicant should express interest in poultry rearing and be willing to attend the full 7-day training session.\n\n<br>\n\n",
  "exclusions": "<br>\n\n",
